From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:43:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pci: retain routes across guest BAR relocation

Port Droid-VM da647254c2a9c6458ac2f5e0d15fb4c33c6333a8. Keep
conflicting BAR moves pending until the previous decoder moves,
and remove stale mappings when a BAR moves with decoding disabled.
Keep the desktop firmware battery page outside the PCI window;
other profiles retain their allocation policy.

BUG=None
TEST=BAR overlap and disabled-decoder relocation unit test on ARM64

Purpose: Retain routes across guest BAR relocation.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
